      "body": "{\"body\":\"Local councils should consider the needs of the whole neighbourhood before deciding how to use public land. A community garden can bring neighbours together and give residents a practical way to grow food. It may also provide a calm place for older people and families. However, an outdoor sports facility can support exercise and give young people a safe place to meet. In my view, the best choice depends on what the area already has. If there is no nearby place for exercise, a small court may be more useful. Where sports facilities are already available, a garden could serve a different need. Councils should consult residents, review available space, and choose a plan that can be maintained over time. The local council could also arrange a trial and review attendance before making a permanent decision.\",\"version\":2}",
